 dye density).","Characteristic curves: x axis is absolute log exposure in lux-seconds (daylight), as printed, axis -4.0 to 1.0; the curves are drawn from about -3.74 to about 0.26. Printed 'Log H ref: -1.74'; the traced r density there is 0.91.","Spectral sensitivity: effective exposure 1/200 s, density 0.2 above D-min, Status M, process C-41; y is log sensitivity (reciprocal exposure in erg/cm2) as printed, the axis runs 0.0 to 4.0. The magenta-forming (g) curve has a blue shoulder (about 1.2 to 1.4 between 395 and 470 nm) before its green peak; the yellow-forming (b) curve starts at about 370 nm, g at about 390 nm and the cyan-forming (r) curve at about 490 nm.","Spectral-dye-density plot has only 'Midscale Neutral' (mid, drawn dashed) and 'Minimum Density' (min), no separate c/m/y dyes; the dashed curve is read through its dashes, so its coverage is about 0.68.","Printed checks (Status M red-filter densities of a normally exposed negative, EI 800): grey card 0.75 to 0.95; lightest paper-gray-scale step 1.00 to 1.20. The sheet also lists EI 1600 (push 1): 0.85 to 1.05 and 1.20 to 1.40.","Grain: Print Grain Index for 135 at 4x6 print (48); only that size is listed. The sheet says the film is optimized for printing on Kodak Ektacolor Edge Paper, Kodak Royal Digital Color Paper and Kodak Professional Endura Metallic Paper."],"print":"kodak-endura-premier","grain":{"grain":27.0,"grain_size":38.0,"grain_roughness":50.0}}